config AX630C_WATCHDOG
	bool "Axera AX630C (AX620E) watchdog"
	depends on ARM64 || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on OF
	select MFD_SYSCON
	select WATCHDOG_CORE
	help
	  Watchdog driver for the Axera AX630C and the rest of the AX620E
	  family. The block interrupts on its first expiry and resets the SoC
	  on the second; its counter clock, gates and resets live in the
	  peripheral syscon rather than in the block itself.

	  On these SoCs the firmware implements no PSCI SYSTEM_RESET, so this
	  block is also the last-resort reboot path, and the bootloader arms it
	  before entering the kernel. Say Y if you are building a kernel for an
	  AX620E-family SoC: there is no module option, because a kernel that
	  reaches modprobe later than the bootloader's timeout never gets there.
